      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Object Rotation\n\nRotate the `<object>` to show the `<view>` side.\n\n**Prompt Template:**\n\n```text\nRotate the <object> to show the <view> side view.\n```\n\n### Supported `<view>` Values\n\n- `front`\n- `right`\n- `left`\n- `rear`\n- `front right`\n- `front left`\n- `rear right`\n- `rear left`\n\n### Example\n\n```text\nRotate the chair to show the rear side view.\n```"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 66,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1520.0613163118105,
        239.6745419442148
      ],
      "size": [
        628.8399999999999,
        846.5000000000002
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Camera Control\n\nUse this pattern to change only the camera viewpoint while keeping the 3D scene unchanged.\n\n**Prompt Template:**\n\n```text\nMove the camera.\n- Camera rotation: Yaw <y_rotation>°, Pitch <p_rotation>°.\n- Camera zoom: <zoom>.\n- Keep the 3D scene static; only change the viewpoint.\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `<y_rotation>` — Camera yaw rotation in degrees.\n- `<p_rotation>` — Camera pitch rotation in degrees.\n- `<zoom>` — One of:\n  - `in`\n  - `out`\n  - `unchanged`\n\n> **Note:** The final line is important. It instructs the model to preserve the scene's geometry and content while changing only the camera viewpoint.\n\n### Example\n\n```text\nMove the camera.\n- Camera rotation: Yaw 45°, Pitch 0°.\n- Camera zoom: in.\n- Keep the 3D scene static; only change the viewpoint.\n```"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
